IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- coa21-ch3-squeeze-out.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 28, Chapter 3 -- "Squeeze-out" (ss 979 to 982).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Reading a result: see the header of coa21-ch1-panel.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING).
-- The shares are modelled as BLOCKS (a class, a value, the votes it carries, how the offeror stands to it), because section 979 counts them
-- differently by status (acceptances, other acquisitions, associates, conditional contracts) and by date. 90% is compared by cross-multiplication.
-- Months: "beginning with D" ends the day before the corresponding date, or on the last day of the month where there is none (fork F3 in NOTES.md); "from D" uses `add months`; six weeks are 42 days.

§ `Part 28, Chapter 3: "Squeeze-out" and "Sell-out"`

§§ `The right of the offeror to buy out a minority shareholder (s 979)`

-- How the offeror stands to a block of the shares to which the offer relates.
DECLARE `s 979 acquisition status` IS ONE OF
    `s 979 acquired or unconditionally contracted to be acquired by virtue of acceptances of the offer`
    `s 979 acquired or unconditionally contracted to be acquired by the offeror otherwise than by virtue of acceptances`
    `s 979 acquired or unconditionally contracted to be acquired by an associate of the offeror`
    `s 979 contracted to be acquired subject to conditions, not yet unconditional`
    `s 979 not acquired or contracted to be acquired`

-- src:13614 | (2) If the offeror has, by virtue of acceptances of the offer, acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire—
-- src:13615 | (a) not less than 90% in value of the shares to which the offer relates, and
-- src:13616 | (b) in a case where the shares to which the offer relates are voting shares, not less than 90% of the voting rights carried by those shares,
-- src:13617 | he may give notice to the holder of any shares to which the offer relates which the offeror has not acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire that he desires to acquire those shares.
-- src:13618 | (3) Subsection (4) applies in a case where a takeover offer relates to shares of different classes.
-- src:13619 | (4) If the offeror has, by virtue of acceptances of the offer, acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire—
-- src:13620 | (a) not less than 90% in value of the shares of any class to which the offer relates, and
-- src:13621 | (b) in a case where the shares of that class are voting shares, not less than 90% of the voting rights carried by those shares,
-- src:13622 | he may give notice to the holder of any shares of that class to which the offer relates which the offeror has not acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire that he desires to acquire those shares.
-- src:13623 | (5) In the case of a takeover offer which includes among the shares to which it relates—
-- src:13624 | (a) shares that are allotted after the date of the offer, or
-- src:13625 | (b) relevant treasury shares (within the meaning of section 974) that cease to be held as treasury shares after the date of the offer,
-- src:13626 | the offeror's entitlement to give a notice under subsection (2) or (4) on any particular date shall be determined as if the shares to which the offer relates did not include any allotted, or ceasing to be held as treasury shares, on or after that date.
-- src:13627 | (6) Subsection (7) applies where—
-- src:13628 | (a) the requirements for the giving of a notice under subsection (2) or (4) are satisfied, and
-- src:13629 | (b) there are shares in the company which the offeror, or an associate of his, has contracted to acquire subject to conditions being met, and in relation to which the contract has not become unconditional.
-- src:13630 | (7) The offeror's entitlement to give a notice under subsection (2) or (4) shall be determined as if—
-- src:13631 | (a) the shares to which the offer relates included shares falling within paragraph (b) of subsection (6), and
-- src:13632 | (b) in relation to shares falling within that paragraph, the words “by virtue of acceptances of the offer” in subsection (2) or (4) were omitted.
-- src:13633 | (8) Where—
-- src:13634 | (a) a takeover offer is made,
-- src:13635 | (b) during the period beginning with the date of the offer and ending when the offer can no longer be accepted, the offeror—
-- src:13636 | (i) acquires or unconditionally contracts to acquire any of the shares to which the offer relates, but
-- src:13637 | (ii) does not do so by virtue of acceptances of the offer, and
-- src:13638 | (c) subsection (10) applies,
-- src:13639 | then for the purposes of this section those shares are not excluded by section 977(1) from those to which the offer relates, and the offeror is treated as having acquired or contracted to acquire them by virtue of acceptances of the offer.
-- src:13640 | (9) Where—
-- src:13641 | (a) a takeover offer is made,
-- src:13642 | (b) during the period beginning with the date of the offer and ending when the offer can no longer be accepted, an associate of the offeror acquires or unconditionally contracts to acquire any of the shares to which the offer relates, and
-- src:13643 | (c) subsection (10) applies,
-- src:13644 | then for the purposes of this section those shares are not excluded by section 977(2) from those to which the offer relates.
@ref s 979(2), (4), (8) and (9) The shares counted, by how the offeror stands to them (src:13614-13644)
DECLARE `s 979 block of shares` HAS
    `s 979 class of the shares` IS A STRING
    `s 979 value of the block` IS A NUMBER
    `s 979 voting rights carried by the block` IS A NUMBER
    `s 979 date the block was allotted after the date of the offer, or ceased to be held as treasury shares after it` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `s 979 status of the block` IS A `s 979 acquisition status`
    `s 979 subsection (10) applies to the acquisition of the block` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `s 979 treatment of a block` IS ONE OF
    `s 979 counts as shares to which the offer relates, acquired by virtue of acceptances`
    `s 979 counts as shares to which the offer relates only`
    `s 979 does not count as shares to which the offer relates`

-- s 979(10): this subsection applies if the acquisition consideration does not exceed the value of the consideration in the terms of the offer, or the terms are revised so that it no longer does.
-- src:13645 | (10) This subsection applies if—
-- src:13646 | (a) at the time the shares are acquired or contracted to be acquired as mentioned in subsection (8) or (9) (as the case may be), the value of the consideration for which they are acquired or contracted to be acquired (“the acquisition consideration”) does not exceed the value of the consideration specified in the terms of the offer, or
-- src:13647 | (b) those terms are subsequently revised so that when the revision is announced the value of the acquisition consideration, at the time mentioned in paragraph (a), no longer exceeds the value of the consideration specified in those terms.
@ref s 979(10) Right of offeror to buy out minority shareholder (src:13645-13647)
GIVEN `the value of the consideration for which the shares are acquired or contracted to be acquired (the acquisition consideration)` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the consideration specified in the terms of the offer` IS A NUMBER
      `the terms are subsequently revised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the consideration specified in the revised terms when the revision is announced` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 979(10) this subsection applies` MEANS
    IF `the value of the consideration for which the shares are acquired or contracted to be acquired (the acquisition consideration)` AT MOST `the value of the consideration specified in the terms of the offer`
       OR (`the terms are subsequently revised` AND `the value of the consideration for which the shares are acquired or contracted to be acquired (the acquisition consideration)` AT MOST `the value of the consideration specified in the revised terms when the revision is announced`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection applies if— (a) at the time the shares are acquired or contracted to be acquired as mentioned in subsection (8) or (9) (as the case may be), the value of the consideration for which they are acquired or contracted to be acquired (“the acquisition consideration”) does not exceed the value of the consideration specified in the terms of the offer"

-- s 979(8): shares the offeror acquires during the offer otherwise than by acceptances are not excluded by section 977(1), and are treated as acquired by acceptances, where subsection (10) applies.
-- src:13633 | (8) Where—
-- src:13634 | (a) a takeover offer is made,
-- src:13635 | (b) during the period beginning with the date of the offer and ending when the offer can no longer be accepted, the offeror—
-- src:13636 | (i) acquires or unconditionally contracts to acquire any of the shares to which the offer relates, but
-- src:13637 | (ii) does not do so by virtue of acceptances of the offer, and
-- src:13638 | (c) subsection (10) applies,
-- src:13639 | then for the purposes of this section those shares are not excluded by section 977(1) from those to which the offer relates, and the offeror is treated as having acquired or contracted to acquire them by virtue of acceptances of the offer.
@ref s 979(8) Right of offeror to buy out minority shareholder (src:13633-13639)
GIVEN `s 979(10) this subsection applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 979(8) the shares are not excluded by section 977(1) and are treated as acquired by virtue of acceptances` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 979(10) this subsection applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where— (a) a takeover offer is made, (b) during the period beginning with the date of the offer and ending when the offer can no longer be accepted, the offeror— (i) acquires or unconditionally contracts to acquire any of the shares to which the offer relates, but (ii) does not do so by virtue of acceptances of the offer, and (c) subsection (10) applies"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether subsection (10) applies is not known

