GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 979(9) the shares are not excluded by section 977(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 979(10) this subsection applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where— (a) a takeover offer is made, (b) during the period beginning with the date of the offer and ending when the offer can no longer be accepted, an associate of the offeror acquires or unconditionally contracts to acquire any of the shares to which the offer relates, and (c) subsection (10) applies"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether subsection (10) applies is not known

-- s 979(5): the offeror's entitlement on a date is determined as if the shares to which the offer relates did not include shares allotted, or ceasing to be treasury shares, on or after that date.
-- src:13623 | (5) In the case of a takeover offer which includes among the shares to which it relates—
-- src:13624 | (a) shares that are allotted after the date of the offer, or
-- src:13625 | (b) relevant treasury shares (within the meaning of section 974) that cease to be held as treasury shares after the date of the offer,
-- src:13626 | the offeror's entitlement to give a notice under subsection (2) or (4) on any particular date shall be determined as if the shares to which the offer relates did not include any allotted, or ceasing to be held as treasury shares, on or after that date.
@ref s 979(5) Right of offeror to buy out minority shareholder (src:13623-13626)
GIVEN block IS A `s 979 block of shares`
      `the date on which the entitlement is determined` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 979(5) the block is among the shares to which the offer relates on the date` MEANS
    CONSIDER block's `s 979 date the block was allotted after the date of the offer, or ceased to be held as treasury shares after it`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        IF d AT LEAST `the date on which the entitlement is determined`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the offeror's entitlement to give a notice under subsection (2) or (4) on any particular date shall be determined as if the shares to which the offer relates did not include any allotted, or ceasing to be held as treasury shares, on or after that date"
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- How a block counts when the entitlement is determined (sections 977, 979(5), (7), (8) and (9) together).
-- src:13623 | (5) In the case of a takeover offer which includes among the shares to which it relates—
-- src:13624 | (a) shares that are allotted after the date of the offer, or
-- src:13625 | (b) relevant treasury shares (within the meaning of section 974) that cease to be held as treasury shares after the date of the offer,
-- src:13626 | the offeror's entitlement to give a notice under subsection (2) or (4) on any particular date shall be determined as if the shares to which the offer relates did not include any allotted, or ceasing to be held as treasury shares, on or after that date.
-- src:13627 | (6) Subsection (7) applies where—
-- src:13628 | (a) the requirements for the giving of a notice under subsection (2) or (4) are satisfied, and
-- src:13629 | (b) there are shares in the company which the offeror, or an associate of his, has contracted to acquire subject to conditions being met, and in relation to which the contract has not become unconditional.
-- src:13630 | (7) The offeror's entitlement to give a notice under subsection (2) or (4) shall be determined as if—
-- src:13631 | (a) the shares to which the offer relates included shares falling within paragraph (b) of subsection (6), and
-- src:13632 | (b) in relation to shares falling within that paragraph, the words “by virtue of acceptances of the offer” in subsection (2) or (4) were omitted.
-- src:13633 | (8) Where—
-- src:13634 | (a) a takeover offer is made,
-- src:13635 | (b) during the period beginning with the date of the offer and ending when the offer can no longer be accepted, the offeror—
-- src:13636 | (i) acquires or unconditionally contracts to acquire any of the shares to which the offer relates, but
-- src:13637 | (ii) does not do so by virtue of acceptances of the offer, and
-- src:13638 | (c) subsection (10) applies,
-- src:13639 | then for the purposes of this section those shares are not excluded by section 977(1) from those to which the offer relates, and the offeror is treated as having acquired or contracted to acquire them by virtue of acceptances of the offer.
-- src:13640 | (9) Where—
-- src:13641 | (a) a takeover offer is made,
-- src:13642 | (b) during the period beginning with the date of the offer and ending when the offer can no longer be accepted, an associate of the offeror acquires or unconditionally contracts to acquire any of the shares to which the offer relates, and
-- src:13643 | (c) subsection (10) applies,
-- src:13644 | then for the purposes of this section those shares are not excluded by section 977(2) from those to which the offer relates.
@ref s 979(5), (7), (8) and (9) How a block of the shares counts (src:13623-13644)
GIVEN block IS A `s 979 block of shares`
      `the date on which the entitlement is determined` IS A DATE
      `conditional contracts are counted among the shares to which the offer relates (subsection (7))` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 979 treatment of a block`
`s 979 how the block counts` MEANS
    IF `s 979(5) the block is among the shares to which the offer relates on the date` block `the date on which the entitlement is determined` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN `s 979 does not count as shares to which the offer relates`
    ELSE CONSIDER block's `s 979 status of the block`
         WHEN `s 979 acquired or unconditionally contracted to be acquired by virtue of acceptances of the offer` THEN `s 979 counts as shares to which the offer relates, acquired by virtue of acceptances`
         WHEN `s 979 acquired or unconditionally contracted to be acquired by the offeror otherwise than by virtue of acceptances` THEN
             IF `s 979(8) the shares are not excluded by section 977(1) and are treated as acquired by virtue of acceptances` `the answer under subsection (10)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             THEN `s 979 counts as shares to which the offer relates, acquired by virtue of acceptances`
             ELSE `s 979 does not count as shares to which the offer relates`
         WHEN `s 979 acquired or unconditionally contracted to be acquired by an associate of the offeror` THEN
             IF `s 979(9) the shares are not excluded by section 977(2)` `the answer under subsection (10)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             THEN `s 979 counts as shares to which the offer relates only`
             ELSE `s 979 does not count as shares to which the offer relates`
         WHEN `s 979 contracted to be acquired subject to conditions, not yet unconditional` THEN
             IF `conditional contracts are counted among the shares to which the offer relates (subsection (7))`
             THEN `s 979 counts as shares to which the offer relates only`
             ELSE `s 979 does not count as shares to which the offer relates`
         WHEN `s 979 not acquired or contracted to be acquired` THEN `s 979 counts as shares to which the offer relates only`
    WHERE
        `the answer under subsection (10)` MEANS IF block's `s 979 subsection (10) applies to the acquisition of the block` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 979(2)(a)-(b) and (4)(a)-(b): not less than 90% in value of the shares, and (for voting shares) not less than 90% of the voting rights carried by them.
-- src:13614 | (2) If the offeror has, by virtue of acceptances of the offer, acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire—
-- src:13615 | (a) not less than 90% in value of the shares to which the offer relates, and
-- src:13616 | (b) in a case where the shares to which the offer relates are voting shares, not less than 90% of the voting rights carried by those shares,
-- src:13617 | he may give notice to the holder of any shares to which the offer relates which the offeror has not acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire that he desires to acquire those shares.
-- src:13618 | (3) Subsection (4) applies in a case where a takeover offer relates to shares of different classes.
-- src:13619 | (4) If the offeror has, by virtue of acceptances of the offer, acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire—
-- src:13620 | (a) not less than 90% in value of the shares of any class to which the offer relates, and
-- src:13621 | (b) in a case where the shares of that class are voting shares, not less than 90% of the voting rights carried by those shares,
-- src:13622 | he may give notice to the holder of any shares of that class to which the offer relates which the offeror has not acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire that he desires to acquire those shares.
@ref s 979(2)(a)-(b) and (4)(a)-(b) The 90% requirements (src:13614-13622)
GIVEN blocks IS A LIST OF `s 979 block of shares`
      `the date on which the entitlement is determined` IS A DATE
      `conditional contracts are counted among the shares to which the offer relates (subsection (7))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are voting shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 979(2)(a)-(b) the 90% requirements are met` MEANS
        `the value of the shares to which the offer relates` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the value acquired or unconditionally contracted to be acquired by virtue of acceptances` TIMES 10 AT LEAST `the value of the shares to which the offer relates` TIMES 9
    AND ((NOT (`the shares are voting shares`)) OR (`the voting rights carried by the shares to which the offer relates` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the voting rights carried by the shares acquired by virtue of acceptances` TIMES 10 AT LEAST `the voting rights carried by the shares to which the offer relates` TIMES 9))
    WHERE
        `how a block counts` b MEANS `s 979 how the block counts` b `the date on which the entitlement is determined` `conditional contracts are counted among the shares to which the offer relates (subsection (7))`
        `the value of the shares to which the offer relates` MEANS
            sum (map (GIVEN b YIELD IF `how a block counts` b EQUALS `s 979 does not count as shares to which the offer relates` THEN 0 ELSE b's `s 979 value of the block`) blocks)
        `the value acquired or unconditionally contracted to be acquired by virtue of acceptances` MEANS
            sum (map (GIVEN b YIELD IF `how a block counts` b EQUALS `s 979 counts as shares to which the offer relates, acquired by virtue of acceptances` THEN b's `s 979 value of the block` ELSE 0) blocks)
        `the voting rights carried by the shares to which the offer relates` MEANS
            sum (map (GIVEN b YIELD IF `how a block counts` b EQUALS `s 979 does not count as shares to which the offer relates` THEN 0 ELSE b's `s 979 voting rights carried by the block`) blocks)
        `the voting rights carried by the shares acquired by virtue of acceptances` MEANS
            sum (map (GIVEN b YIELD IF `how a block counts` b EQUALS `s 979 counts as shares to which the offer relates, acquired by virtue of acceptances` THEN b's `s 979 voting rights carried by the block` ELSE 0) blocks)

-- s 979(6): subsection (7) applies where the requirements for giving a notice are satisfied and shares are contracted for subject to conditions not yet unconditional.
-- src:13627 | (6) Subsection (7) applies where—
-- src:13628 | (a) the requirements for the giving of a notice under subsection (2) or (4) are satisfied, and
-- src:13629 | (b) there are shares in the company which the offeror, or an associate of his, has contracted to acquire subject to conditions being met, and in relation to which the contract has not become unconditional.
@ref s 979(6) Right of offeror to buy out minority shareholder (src:13627-13629)
GIVEN `the requirements for the giving of a notice under subsection (2) or (4) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are shares which the offeror, or an associate of his, has contracted to acquire subject to conditions being met, and the contract has not become unconditional` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 979(6) subsection (7) applies` MEANS
    IF `the requirements for the giving of a notice under subsection (2) or (4) are satisfied` AND `there are shares which the offeror, or an associate of his, has contracted to acquire subject to conditions being met, and the contract has not become unconditional`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (7) applies where— (a) the requirements for the giving of a notice under subsection (2) or (4) are satisfied, and (b) there are shares in the company which the offeror, or an associate of his, has contracted to acquire subject to conditions being met"

-- s 979(1): subsection (2) applies in a case where the offer does not relate to shares of different classes; s 979(3): subsection (4) applies where it does.
-- src:13613 | (1) Subsection (2) applies in a case where a takeover offer does not relate to shares of different classes.
@ref s 979(1) Right of offeror to buy out minority shareholder (src:13613-13613)
GIVEN `the takeover offer relates to shares of different classes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 979(1) subsection (2) applies` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the takeover offer relates to shares of different classes`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) applies in a case where a takeover offer does not relate to shares of different classes."

-- src:13618 | (3) Subsection (4) applies in a case where a takeover offer relates to shares of different classes.
@ref s 979(3) Right of offeror to buy out minority shareholder (src:13618-13618)
GIVEN `the takeover offer relates to shares of different classes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 979(3) subsection (4) applies` MEANS
    IF `the takeover offer relates to shares of different classes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (4) applies in a case where a takeover offer relates to shares of different classes."

-- s 979(2) and (4): the offeror may give notice to the holder of shares not acquired that he desires to acquire them.
