      `the day the consideration was received` IS A DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
      `the company is wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 982(5) this subsection applies` MEANS
    IF `reasonable enquiries have been made at reasonable intervals to find the person` AND (`the day` AT LEAST (`add years` `the day the consideration was received` 12) OR `the company is wound up`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection applies where— (a) reasonable enquiries have been made at reasonable intervals to find the person, and (b) twelve years have elapsed since the consideration was received, or the company is wound up."

-- s 982(4): if the person entitled cannot be found and subsection (5) applies, the consideration must be paid into court (not for a company registered in Scotland, where (7) and (8) apply instead).
-- src:13697 | (4) If—
-- src:13698 | (a) the person entitled to the consideration held on trust by virtue of section 981(9) cannot be found, and
-- src:13699 | (b) subsection (5) applies,
-- src:13700 | the consideration (together with any interest, dividend or other benefit that has accrued from it) must be paid into court.
-- src:13701 | (5) This subsection applies where—
-- src:13702 | (a) reasonable enquiries have been made at reasonable intervals to find the person, and
-- src:13703 | (b) twelve years have elapsed since the consideration was received, or the company is wound up.
-- src:13704 | (6) In relation to a company registered in Scotland, subsections (7) and (8) apply instead of subsection (4).
@ref s 982(4) and (6) Payment into court, or for Scotland subsections (7) and (8) (src:13697-13704)
GIVEN `the person entitled to the consideration held on trust by virtue of section 981(9) cannot be found` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 982(5) this subsection applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 982(4) the consideration must be paid into court` MEANS
    IF place EQUALS `Scotland`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In relation to a company registered in Scotland, subsections (7) and (8) apply instead of subsection (4)."
    ELSE IF `the person entitled to the consideration held on trust by virtue of section 981(9) cannot be found` AND `s 982(5) this subsection applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If— (a) the person entitled to the consideration held on trust by virtue of section 981(9) cannot be found, and (b) subsection (5) applies"

-- s 982(7): for a company registered in Scotland, the trust terminates, the company or liquidator must sell non-cash consideration, and the sum must be deposited in the name of the Accountant of Court.
-- src:13705 | (7) If the person entitled to the consideration held on trust by virtue of section 981(9) cannot be found and subsection (5) applies—
-- src:13706 | (a) the trust terminates,
-- src:13707 | (b) the company or (if the company is wound up) the liquidator must sell any consideration other than cash and any benefit other than cash that has accrued from the consideration, and
-- src:13708 | (c) a sum representing—
-- src:13709 | (i) the consideration so far as it is cash,
-- src:13710 | (ii) the proceeds of any sale under paragraph (b), and
-- src:13711 | (iii) any interest, dividend or other benefit that has accrued from the consideration,
-- src:13712 | must be deposited in the name of the Accountant of Court in a separate bank account complying with subsection (3) and the receipt for the deposit must be transmitted to the Accountant of Court.
@ref s 982(7) Further provision about consideration held on trust under section 981(9) (src:13705-13712)
GIVEN `the person entitled to the consideration held on trust by virtue of section 981(9) cannot be found` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 982(5) this subsection applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 982(7) the trust terminates and the sum must be deposited in the name of the Accountant of Court` MEANS
    IF place EQUALS `Scotland` AND `the person entitled to the consideration held on trust by virtue of section 981(9) cannot be found` AND `s 982(5) this subsection applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsections (7) and (8) apply "In relation to a company registered in Scotland", where the person cannot be found and subsection (5) applies

-- s 982(8): section 150 of the Bankruptcy (Scotland) Act 2016 applies, so far as consistent with this Act, to sums deposited under subsection (7).
-- src:13713 | (8) Section 150 of the Bankruptcy (Scotland) Act 2016 (so far as consistent with this Act) applies (with any necessary modifications) to sums deposited under subsection (7) as it applies to sums deposited under section 148(3) of that Act.
@ref s 982(8) Further provision about consideration held on trust under section 981(9) (src:13713-13713)
GIVEN `s 982(7) the trust terminates and the sum must be deposited in the name of the Accountant of Court` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 982(8) section 150 of the Bankruptcy (Scotland) Act 2016 applies to the sum` MEANS
    IF `s 982(7) the trust terminates and the sum must be deposited in the name of the Accountant of Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE -- (so far as consistent with this Act, and with any necessary modifications)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section applies to "sums deposited under subsection (7)"

